🔶 **Bug** | Major

**Malformed charge event is 400'd, never stored.** parse(ChargeSucceeded, event.data) throws an HttpError 400 inside tx, which rolls back, so a signed charge.succeeded without invoice metadata is never written to webhook_events. The provider will keep retrying it. The PR says every event is stored and non-fitting ones are `ignored`. Use safeParse and fall back to `ignored`.

<sub>Test to extend: `test/webhooks.test.ts:99` — add the case this comment describes</sub>

```suggestion
        if (event.type === 'charge.succeeded') {
          const charge = ChargeSucceeded.safeParse(event.data);
          if (charge.success) outcome = applyChargeSucceeded(db, charge.data, receivedAt);
        }
```

